KG42.register("rules-bd16d5e73fc8467d2302dd01",{"id":"31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R005","paper":"31-coalition_formation","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R005","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Consumer participation","process_stage":"participation","market_meaning":"A prosumer may purchase its deficient energy from other prosumers in the network. Scope: Buying deficient energy within the considered P2P network. A state 1 prosumer buys energy only when necessary to meet its energy deficiency. Scope: Demand-side participation of state 1 prosumers. Condition: The prosumer is in state 1. A state 2 prosumer may buy energy from other peers to charge its battery for future needs. Scope: Demand-side participation of state 2 prosumers in peer energy trading. Condition: The prosumer is in state 2.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function participation.consumer under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["participation.consumer"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"participation","context_text":"Buying deficient energy within the considered P2P network. | Demand-side participation of state 1 prosumers. | Demand-side participation of state 2 prosumers in peer energy trading.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E003","v141-b-g01-E008","v141-b-g01-E009"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"A prosumer may purchase its deficient energy from other prosumers in the network. Scope: Buying deficient energy within the considered P2P network.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.consumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E008"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"A state 1 prosumer buys energy only when necessary to meet its energy deficiency. Scope: Demand-side participation of state 1 prosumers. Condition: The prosumer is in state 1.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.consumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E009"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"A state 2 prosumer may buy energy from other peers to charge its battery for future needs. Scope: Demand-side participation of state 2 prosumers in peer energy trading. Condition: The prosumer is in state 2.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.consumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E003","v141-b-g01-E009"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E003","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"1. Introduction","anchor_text":"al- prosumers. In particular, we use the framework of a cooperative game to [30] to capture the inte","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"State 1 refers to the state of a prosumer, in which it does not charge or discharge its battery for participating in P2P trading. It only uses its surplus generation for participating in the market. State 2 of a prosumer, on the other hand, refers to the state, in which it is willing to charge or discharge its battery for buying energy from or selling energy to the P2P market."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E008","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p03-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"2. System model","anchor_text":"cordingly, d n,sur ( t ) = ( En ,pv (t ) + En,dis ( t )) ( En,hou ( t ) + En ,cha ( t )), (2) u- E a","equation_id":"2-3","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"A prosumer n can sell E_{n,sur}(t) either to the CPS or to other prosumers in set N\\{n\\} of the network and can buy E_{n,def}(t) from either of them. Note that in (2) and (3) the surplus and deficiency are calculated respectively after a prosumer already charges it battery from its own generation and discharges the battery for its household demand."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E009","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"2. System model","anchor_text":"a its battery in the energy trading market. Similarly, a state 1 prosumer in only buys energy, when ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table 1","image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We further consider that the prosumers participating in the P2P energy trading choose to be either of the two states at any given time slot t.\n(a) State 1 Prosumers in state 1 do not charge or discharge their batteries for trading purposes and only sell their surplus E_{n,sur}(t) to other prosumers in N\\{n\\} or to the grid when E_{n,sur}(t) = (E_{n,hou}(t) + E_{n,cha}(t)) - E_{n,pv}(t) > 0. In other words, a prosumer in state 1, which we denote as an element of set W, does not put its battery in the energy trading market. Similarly, a state 1 prosumer only buys energy, when necessary, to meet the deficient energy E_{n,def}(t) = (E_{n,pv}(t) + E_{n,dis}(t)) - E_{n,hou}(t). Note that a prosumer without any battery always remains in state 1.\n(b) State 2 Prosumers is state 2 use their batteries for trading purposes. That is, a prosumer in state 2, which we indicate via V is motivated, e.g., for more economical benefit, to discharge its battery for selling energy to other prosumers. Similarly, it may also buy energy from other peers to charge its battery for future needs.\nNote that when a prosumer does not have a battery (prosumer 6) or it does not want to charge or discharge despite having battery (prosumer 5 in time slot 1) will remain in state 1."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"This participation rule introduces no design selection or operational decision variable. It states who may buy under state conditions; state membership and E_{n,def}(t) are source quantities defined or used in other rule scopes and are not declared as typed x objects in this frozen rule. Adding them here would relocate cross-rule facts rather than formalize this rule.","empty_theta_reason":"The rule introduces no fixed parameter, coefficient, numeric value, or constant with a source-supported value for this scope. The quotations mention state labels and deficiency quantities, but they do not define a fixed theta object or domain for R005."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"participation.consumer","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E008","quote":"A prosumer n can sell E_{n,sur}(t) either to the CPS or to other prosumers in set N\\{n\\} of the network and can buy E_{n,def}(t) from either of them."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E009","quote":"Similarly, a state 1 prosumer only buys energy, when necessary, to meet the deficient energy E_{n,def}(t)"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E009","quote":"Similarly, it may also buy energy from other peers to charge its battery for future needs."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E003","quote":"State 2 of a prosumer, on the other hand, refers to the state, in which it is willing to charge or discharge its battery for buying energy from or selling energy to the P2P market."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"db1cf2f8282d65a2facffc4f45588d1b62c0f7f22ec05ae7e001d376246c7645","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The frozen rule states procedural demand-side participation conditions: a prosumer may buy deficient energy from peers, state 1 prosumers buy only when necessary to meet deficiency, and state 2 prosumers may buy peer energy to charge a battery. The supplied B quotations define the two states and state that E_{n,def}(t) can be bought from peers or the CPS, but they do not provide an equation, inequality, or optimization constraint specific to this participation rule. The quantitative expressions for surplus/deficiency belong to other rule scopes and are not a participation constraint here. B evidence remains unreviewed; this assessment uses only the supplied quotations and does not assert independent source verification.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","node_ids":["participation.consumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The constraint is a qualitative consumer/prosumer participation condition owned by participation.consumer. No graph edge is asserted because the frozen E set for this rule is empty."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","node_ids":["participation.consumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The state-1 demand-side participation condition is attached to the rule's sole approved node, participation.consumer; the frozen graph provides no further typed nodes or edges for this procedural branch."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C003","node_ids":["participation.consumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The state-2 demand-side participation condition is attached to participation.consumer. The source quotation supports the behavior qualitatively, while the frozen graph has no edge or typed state object for a formal expression."}],"revision_requests":["No graph revision is required to retain the source's procedural participation rule. If a quantitative formalization is required, C.1 must add typed objects for state membership and peer-purchased energy with domains/units, and resolve the discrepancy between the state-1 deficiency expression printed in v141-b-g01-E009 and equation (3)."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
